Running Your Own Copy

You may run your own copy of the software, changed or not, for yourself and
the people you play with (your table). Everyone at your table may use that
copy. It must not be offered to the public: no open sign-up, no listing or
advertising it, and no one outside your table invited to use it.

Permitted Purpose

A permitted purpose is any purpose other than a commercial one. You may not:

- sell the software, or a copy, change or new work based on it;
- charge for access to it, or for anything it does;
- run advertising, sponsorship, donations or paid features on or around it;
- use any part of it to train or improve machine-learning or artificial
